1. MANDATORY PROBLEM STATEMENT
================================================================

Develop an AI-driven civic intelligence solution that enables local authorities, housing societies, and ward-level teams to turn raw air-quality data into actionable local interventions.

The app must use Generative AI as a real core component to interpret pasted or uploaded messy data tables with inconsistent formats, units, dates, headers, and missing readings. It must summarize trends and likely hotspots in plain language.

It must recommend prioritized local actions suitable for:

- Ward Officer / local authority
- Housing Society / RWA manager
- School Coordinator / Principal

Every finding must link to underlying data. Missing, unreliable, invalid, duplicate, or questionable readings must be clearly flagged.

Every new briefing must compare against a previous compatible briefing and show what changed.

The app must generate:

- an internal civic briefing note;
- multilingual citizen advisories;
- different reading levels;
- dedicated guidance for children, older adults, and people sensitive to poor air.

The solution must visibly demonstrate this operational chain:

Actual data
→ data validation and anomaly detection
→ traceable evidence
→ real Gemini analysis
→ role-specific action draft
→ head approval
→ targeted local alert
→ action task dispatch
→ completion proof
