7. DETERMINISTIC ANALYTICS AND SCIENTIFIC GUARDRAILS
================================================================

Before Gemini analysis, calculate all numerical facts server-side from eligible readings:

- valid/invalid counts;
- missing-data rate;
- duplicate/outlier rate;
- pollutant/location/time aggregates;
- current/previous comparison;
- trend direction when enough time-series data exists;
- hotspot ranking;
- reliability/confidence score;
- data-quality limitations;
- source-row evidence sets;
- short-term projection only when sufficient comparable history exists.

AQI requirements:

- Compute CPCB AQI only when source measurements and averaging periods support a valid calculation.
- Use highest valid pollutant sub-index as overall AQI.
- If valid AQI cannot be calculated, display:
  “AQI unavailable from supplied data.”
- Never invent AQI.
- Red-zone alert must rely on valid calculated/provided AQI and configured rule.
- Future output must be labelled:
  “Short-term data projection — not a guaranteed forecast.”

Source pattern requirements:

- Use “possible source pattern,” not confirmed source.
- Example labels: possible construction/road dust, possible fine-smoke pattern, possible traffic influence, mixed urban pattern.
- Do-not-do guardrails must come from a reviewed action policy catalog.
- AI may recommend action drafts but cannot issue legally binding orders.

